  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between Divaricataester C and CCF-STTG1, mediated through a series of enzymatic targets. Divaricataester C is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is then targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds, in turn, target CCF-STTG1, indicating a potential pathway where Divaricataester C may influence the activity of these enzymes, which ultimately affect CCF-STTG1. The evidence suggests that Divaricataester C could act as a modulator of the enzymatic cascade leading to CCF-STTG1, possibly through competitive inhibition or other regulatory mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting the intermediate enzyme CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase as a potential therapeutic strategy.",
